---
import '../styles/evidence-operation.css';
---

<section id="evidence" class="evidence-layer shell" data-evidence-layer aria-labelledby="evidence-title">
  <header class="evidence-heading evidence-reveal">
    <div>
      <span class="evidence-index">03 / evidence & operation</span>
      <h2 id="evidence-title">Design claims are cheap.<br />Operational evidence is not.</h2>
    </div>
    <p>
      This layer ties the previous case studies to concrete repository artifacts, regression history and the runtime
      topology I actually operate. The goal is not to dump implementation details; it is to show where each design
      principle becomes enforceable.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="evidence-trace evidence-reveal" aria-label="Evidence flow">
    <span>claim</span><i></i><span>implementation</span><i></i><span>failure</span><i></i><span>operation</span>
  </div>

  <article class="evidence-system evidence-reveal" id="evidence-minecartainer">
    <header class="evidence-system-header">
      <div>
        <span class="evidence-kind">01 / STATEFUL RUNTIME</span>
        <h3>Minecartainer</h3>
      </div>
      <p>Persistent-state safety is represented by state records, explicit transitions and tests that expect refusal.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="evidence-grid">
      <a class="evidence-record evidence-record-primary" href="https://github.com/AlexanderGG-0520/minecartainer/blob/main/docs/server-install-reinstall-policy.md">
        <span class="record-type">STATE CONTRACT</span>
        <code>/data/.server-install.json</code>
        <strong>Configuration drift fails before managed state is replaced.</strong>
        <p>
          The marker records <code>artifact</code>, <code>type</code>, <code>version</code> and <code>build</code>. A valid
          mismatch fails by default; <code>FORCE_REINSTALL=true</code> is an explicit operator decision and still does not
          delete worlds, mods, plugins or configuration.
        </p>
        <small>server-install-reinstall-policy.md ↗</small>
      </a>

      <a class="evidence-record" href="https://github.com/AlexanderGG-0520/minecartainer/blob/main/scripts/lib/install_phase.sh">
        <span class="record-type">LIFECYCLE</span>
        <code>install()</code>
        <strong>Installation is an explicit phase, not an accidental side effect of every boot.</strong>
        <p>
          Server artifacts, worlds, mods, datapacks, configs and plugins pass through a named install pipeline with
          pre/post boundaries before the runtime takes over.
        </p>
        <small>scripts/lib/install_phase.sh ↗</small>
      </a>

      <a class="evidence-record" href="https://github.com/AlexanderGG-0520/minecartainer/blob/main/.github/workflows/runtime-smoke.yml">
        <span class="record-type">REGRESSION SURFACE</span>
        <code>runtime-smoke.yml</code>
        <strong>Failure paths are executable specifications.</strong>
        <p>
          Runtime CI exercises lifecycle regressions such as install-only behavior, RCON safety, managed marker
          mismatches, bring-your-own artifacts and ownership-sensitive modpack behavior.
        </p>
        <small>GitHub Actions workflow ↗</small>
      </a>

      <div class="evidence-record evidence-record-observed">
        <span class="record-type">KUBERNETES OPERATION</span>
        <code>single writer → graceful stop</code>
        <strong>The world outlives the Pod.</strong>
        <p>
          Maintained deployment patterns use persistent storage, conservative replacement, readiness and a bounded
          Minecraft-aware shutdown path instead of treating the JVM as disposable state.
        </p>
        <small>operational model / documented in repository</small>
      </div>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="evidence-system evidence-reveal" id="evidence-mc-router">
    <header class="evidence-system-header">
      <div>
        <span class="evidence-kind">02 / NETWORK EDGE</span>
        <h3>mc-router</h3>
      </div>
      <p>The strongest evidence is not a feature list. It is a production regression that changed the architecture.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="incident-record" data-incident-record>
      <div class="incident-meta">
        <span>RECOVERY COMMIT</span>
        <code>36c75dc</code>
        <time datetime="2026-08-23">2026-08-23</time>
      </div>
      <div class="incident-copy">
        <span class="incident-state">STATUS ROUTING REGRESSION → RESPONSIBILITY BOUNDARY</span>
        <h4>Restore Java routing semantics and observability.</h4>
        <p>
          Router-owned monitoring state had started influencing Minecraft STATUS behavior. Recovery restored explicit
          precedence — <code>statusOverride → statusBackend → backend</code> — while LOGIN and Transfer stayed on the
          normal backend, and removed monitoring state from STATUS response control.
        </p>
        <a href="https://github.com/AlexanderGG-0520/mc-router/commit/36c75dcb9535a3f5f173cd19f45587490884940e">open recovery commit ↗</a>
      </div>
      <div class="incident-black-case" aria-label="Regression black case">
        <span>BLACK CASE</span>
        <p><b>STATUS</b> canonical host → statusBackend</p>
        <p><b>LOGIN</b> explicit alias → normal backend</p>
        <p><b>FALLBACK</b> must not overwrite healthy statusBackend</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="evidence-grid evidence-grid-router">
      <a class="evidence-record" href="https://github.com/AlexanderGG-0520/mc-router#how-java-routing-works">
        <span class="record-type">PROTOCOL BOUNDARY</span>
        <code>handshake → opaque TCP</code>
        <strong>Parse only what is needed to route.</strong>
        <p>
          Normal Java traffic reads the initial handshake for host identity and next state, forwards the original bytes,
          then stops interpreting gameplay traffic.
        </p>
        <small>routing model ↗</small>
      </a>

      <a class="evidence-record" href="https://github.com/AlexanderGG-0520/mc-router#explicit-yaml-first-discovery-second">
        <span class="record-type">ROUTE MODEL</span>
        <code>static + discovered → snapshot</code>
        <strong>Kubernetes discovery feeds routing; it does not redefine routing semantics.</strong>
        <p>
          Static YAML and discovered Services converge on the same route model so the network core remains testable
          independently of the cluster control plane.
        </p>
        <small>design rationale ↗</small>
      </a>

      <a class="evidence-record" href="https://github.com/AlexanderGG-0520/mc-router#keep-workload-lifecycle-outside-routing-correctness">
        <span class="record-type">CONTROL BOUNDARY</span>
        <code>route decision ≠ lifecycle authority</code>
        <strong>Optional control integrations cannot become implicit route truth.</strong>
        <p>
          Scaler hooks, availability observations and Hub notifications can consume or emit control-plane information
          without silently changing the selected backend.
        </p>
        <small>responsibility boundary ↗</small>
      </a>
    </div>
  </article>

  <article class="evidence-system evidence-reveal" id="evidence-home-platform">
    <header class="evidence-system-header">
      <div>
        <span class="evidence-kind">03 / INFRASTRUCTURE</span>
        <h3>Home Kubernetes Platform</h3>
      </div>
      <p>This evidence is operational rather than a public repository: a real cluster with explicit limits and rebuildable layers.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="runtime-topology" aria-label="Current home platform runtime topology">
      <div class="runtime-host">
        <span>PHYSICAL FAILURE DOMAIN</span>
        <strong>1 host</strong>
        <small>current constraint / not HA</small>
      </div>
      <div class="runtime-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
      <div class="runtime-layer runtime-proxmox">
        <span>VIRTUALIZATION</span>
        <strong>Proxmox VE</strong>
        <small>VM lifecycle boundary</small>
      </div>
      <div class="runtime-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
      <div class="runtime-vms">
        <div><span>CONTROL PLANE VM</span><strong>cp-01</strong><small>cluster control / etcd</small></div>
        <div><span>WORKER VM</span><strong>worker-01</strong><small>application workloads</small></div>
      </div>
      <div class="runtime-arrow" aria-hidden="true">↓</div>
      <div class="runtime-layer runtime-kubernetes">
        <span>APPLICATION PLATFORM</span>
        <strong>Kubernetes</strong>
        <div class="runtime-services">
          <i>Cilium / network</i><i>Longhorn / storage</i><i>Argo CD / delivery</i><i>CRI-O / runtime</i>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="operation-ledger">
      <section>
        <span>REBUILDABILITY</span>
        <strong>From guided install to repeatable procedure.</strong>
        <p>
          The platform stopped being a one-off lab once I could destroy and rebuild it myself and write installation
          procedures for other operators. Reproducibility became part of the platform definition.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span>REAL WORKLOADS</span>
        <strong>Minecraft and web applications share one operating model.</strong>
        <p>
          Stateful game servers and ordinary web services are reconciled by the same cluster while keeping their
          storage, network and shutdown requirements explicit at the workload boundary.
        </p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <span>LIMITATION</span>
        <strong>Logical separation is not physical availability.</strong>
        <p>
          cp-01 and worker-01 are separate VMs, but one physical host still owns the failure domain. The topology is
          designed to expand without presenting the current machine as an HA cluster.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </article>

  <div class="evidence-principle evidence-reveal">
    <span>WHAT THIS LAYER PROVES</span>
    <p>
      The projects are not architecture diagrams assembled after the fact. Their invariants show up in persisted state,
      executable failure cases, recovery commits and infrastructure I have to keep operating.
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="evidence-next evidence-reveal">
    <span>04 / live runtime</span>
    <i></i>
    <span>the running portfolio process becomes evidence next</span>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  import '../scripts/evidence-operation.ts';
</script>
